After playing this game in pre-alpha I can see an insane potential for this game;
Quickly breaking into the "Quake" style genre of games, due its smooth flow and emphasis on movement and snap shot aiming.
The game is ultimately silly (in the best way possible) and will bring hours of fun for a happy and eager customer, whilst some physics can be unstable, the DEVs are working long and hard to make sure this game becomes one of the best therefore making the game easily accessible for a new player, with new features that will be coming out of the next couple days, weeks, months and perhaps years until this game is  100% complete, I've personally not witnessed a more friendly DEV team than the wonderful people that are working on this masterpiece.
Whilst the game has its comedic side, it also has a rather serious side to the game also, in which your team can easily communicate and ultimately PWN the other team due to there being a number of different set-ups your team can have, with the integration of the party function, the game allows the more serious players to group up and head out for some games and get some well earned Tea-bags.
Yes, I said tea-bags, the objective is to tea-bag the opponent.
In conclusion;

Hope this will help other gamers and puzzle platform enthusiasts, have fun! ^.^
Adventures of Shuggy is a really fun, ocazionally frustrating, puzzle platformer. you are the almighty purple vampire batman called Shuggy (don't be intimidated by his ferocious name). Whose newly bought house is being haunted by random monsters. your job is to clear them out...just like ghost busters:D
Cons (most are minor inconveniencies):
- while 90% of the leve's are skill based you will find out that sometimes you will need to be a bit lucky;
- ice floor walking physics can be easily iritating;
- (not 100% sure) has co-op but i don't know for sure if it is also online co-op or just simple coop (aka same keyboard or with controler);
- you will hate mosquitos even more :))
Pros:
- a lot of variety in puzzles, having quite enough elements to make each level diferent and fun (more or less);
- a good number of levels, around 110 or so;
- has co-op;
- challenging yet fulfilling;
- diferent themed level's;

